40. In the case reported in 36 CWN 1002 the Calcutta High Court while deciding the question as to the burden of proof in respect of the ground based on section 27(b) of the Specific Relief Act, 1877 held as under; 

 "where a person claims to be a transferee for value without notice of the original contract, the burden is on him to prove that he fulfils that character." 

 41. We are in humble agreement with the decision of the Calcutta High Court as above. Since the reason for such conclusion lies on the provisions of section 106 of the Evidence Act, 1872 that when any fact is especially within the knowledge of any person, the burden of proving that fact is upon him. But how this burden could be discharged that was decided by their lordship in the Lahore High Court in the case Malik Md Ishaque vs Mirza Almas Ali reported 21 DLR (WP) 333 a follows;
